  "narrative": "The two due claims are now both supported by independent validation and can be closed. For H67, PTEN loss in the TP53-intact and KEAP1-intact eligible population gave discovery +0.255 signed units (discovery lower +0.165) and independent validation +0.305 with strict lower bound +0.166. Because the claimed direction is negative raw exposed-minus-comparator, the signed positive estimates correspond to lower composite dependency scores, i.e. stronger measured dependency. Both estimates exceed the 0.15 threshold and the strict validation lower bound also exceeds it, so H67 is accepted and closed. The inference is dataset-internal and conditional: PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency when TP53 and KEAP1 losses are absent. It does not establish an unconditional PTEN main effect; the broader overall PTEN comparisons remain rejected or non-meaningful.\n\nFor H90, MSI-high status restricted to TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact, and KEAP1-intact lines gave discovery +0.745 signed units (lower +0.666) and independent validation +0.779 with strict lower bound +0.675. Both are far above the 0.15 threshold and directionally stable. Since the claim direction is negative raw, MSI-high lines are associated with stronger measured dependency even after removing the three dominant core predictor contexts. H90 is therefore accepted and closed as one of the strongest supported associations in this supplied dataset. This remains an association, not proof that MSI-high causes dependency or that the effect will generalize externally.\n\nTaken together, the validated supported findings in this dataset are: SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger dependency; KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency; PTEN loss associated with stronger dependency in TP53/KEAP1-intact contexts and also in TP53-intact contexts; MSI-high associated with stronger dependency both overall and after restricting away TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1 loss contexts. The constructed research_signature_b context effect on TP53 loss is also validated as a reversed interaction, but its biological meaning remains uncertain because the assay is constructed and the threshold is analysis-defined. Major negative findings include no meaningful overall lineage-subtype main effect, no meaningful modification of SMARCA4, KEAP1, or TP53 effects by lineage subtype, no meaningful SMARCA4-by-KEAP1 interaction, no meaningful effects for the constructed binary markers, no meaningful overall PTEN, KRAS, MTAP, MYC, ARID1A, BRCA2, NF1, RB1, SMAD4, EGFR, ERBB2, stk11, PIK3CA, or CDKN2A main effects, and no meaningful technical batch/omics-availability confound for matched RNA/DNA availability. Unresolved but lower-priority uncertainty remains around H65, the discovery-only signature_a interaction with TP53 loss; H84, the underpowered direct TP53 stratum inside high signature_b; and several PTEN/CDKN2A/technical context probes. The most informative next analyses are the newly proposed MSI-high conditional main effects within TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and SMARCA4-loss contexts, because they test whether the very strong MSI-high association persists when dominant predictor effects are present rather than only when those predictors are absent. If MSI-high remains meaningful in those contexts, it is a broad dataset association; if it attenuates strongly in one context, context dependence becomes important.",
  "research_notes": "Current strongest supported dataset associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency; H7 KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency; H3 TP53 loss -> weaker dependency; H82 high research_signature_b reverses/attenuates TP53-loss association; H58 and H67 PTEN loss -> stronger dependency in TP53/KEAP1-intact or TP53-intact contexts; H41 overall MSI-high -> stronger dependency; H90 MSI-high -> stronger dependency after removing TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1-loss contexts, now validated and closed. H67 closed. H90 closed. H65 signature_a interaction remains accepted but discovery-only and should be a priority validation candidate if allowed. H84 direct high signature_b TP53 stratum remains unresolved/closed as underpowered; interpret via H82/H85. Lineage-subtype modification of core predictors is not supported (H44/H45/H46 rejected). Constructed binary markers and many mutation main effects are rejected. Technical audits: batch A vs B null, matched RNA/DNA null; remaining technical claims have low priority. CDKN2A-loss estimates remain below or not robustly above the meaningful threshold; treat as negative/uninformative. Next analysis priority: test MSI-high effect within TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and SMARCA4-loss contexts; analyze H83 if valid; consider validating H65 and H51 later. Avoid causal and generalizability language, especially for constructed signatures and threshold-defined interactions."
